{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543222-have-you-had-your-character-do-any-embracing","id":1543222,"title":"Have you had your character do any embracing?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-10-06T15:44:13-07:00","id":1543222,"title":"Have you had your character do any embracing?","content":"I'm just curious as I'm thinking of having my Malkavian possibly doing that down the road if and when he goes back to London England.<br /> <br /> Was it hard or tricky to play two or more different characters or npcs from the same lineage?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-06T17:32:39-07:00","id":1543233,"title":"","content":"Embracing doesn't means you get to play both characters, in fact I never saw this before outside NPCs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-06T19:38:51-07:00","id":1543241,"title":"","content":"I was curious Monteparnas as I never considered having my player character ever taking such a step and then it would be if I felt I done all that I could with the character in our game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-07T00:09:14-07:00","id":1543256,"title":"","content":"The only time I've done it is in larger group games where there's enough players for there to be a lot of vampires and PC ghouls and mortals around to play potential neonates. It's a rather different context from a normal TT style play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-10T12:15:13-07:00","id":1543534,"title":"","content":"in my Transylvania and Giovanni Chronicles I'm trying to make it more feasible and interesting.<br /> Of course, there is the little details like &quot;do vampires feel the need to Embrace?&quot; (which I interpret as Yes), which can be or not focused on.<br /> <br /> But, like, I will make one of my Toreador PC (who is descendant of Michael) be the sire of the first Daughter of Cacophony.<br /> One of my Ventrue PC will be the sire (or at least for now is mentor) of Lucita.<br /> <br /> One of my Players who is very engaged made her Elder Malk have Embraced basically a family of her own, through the years. She also lost a childe to the fires of Inquisition.<br /> And her Tzimisce character started a Revenant family to serve him, but I don't know if it has already Embraced one of them.<br /> <br /> So yeah, I love characters embracing, making their own lineage forward. But the game has always given good reasons NOT to have childer. Both mechanically and narratively. <br /> You get nothing game-wise. That's why I give a free \u2022 Mawla in an Embrace (or the same value if the childer was another Background). To give something. <br /> <br /> In the Narrative, that usually means just one more thing for the Storyteller to backstab you with (since all books just keep asking players to detail their character sheet, and incetivizing STs to request that information just to use it against players). And since there is no practical use, many if not most players won't want to Embrace. There is no incentive, and there is in fact more guaranteed desincentive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-11T20:05:52-07:00","id":1543603,"title":"","content":"Not in the sense you mean, though my most evil character embraced and diablerized a few of an enemy's closest mortal associates and left the bodies piled in their office as a message.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-11T20:34:26-07:00","id":1543605,"title":"","content":"I never really played sadastic monsters in either Vampire game and did it ever cross the comfort level of other players in the game Matt The Bruins Fan?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-12T23:21:40-07:00","id":1543666,"title":"","content":"I think that instance did. At least it spooked the other player into dropping an interesting and well-rounded character in favor of introducing a new one who was designed for combat rather than social situations. In retrospect I wish I hadn't done it for that reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-14T20:33:30-07:00","id":1543823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543222-have-you-had-your-character-do-any-embracing#post1543222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm just curious as I'm thinking of having my Malkavian possibly doing that down the road if and when he goes back to London England.<br /> <br /> Was it hard or tricky to play two or more different characters or npcs from the same lineage?</div> </div> </div> </div>IMO the best way to accomplish this would be to retire the sire character as a ST controlled NPC and play the childe character. If you had been keeping notes for the sire character and have or make a good write up, they should be able to keep the feel of how you played the character thus far and you move on with the childe. Ultimately it would be up to you and the ST if he wants to allow you to play more than one character, though there is a larger chance of meta-gaming their relationship.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","name":"Aydoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-21T09:18:07-07:00","id":1544399,"title":"","content":"I've played three vampire characters who have embraced in game, or, at least in the epilogue. The first was my very first Requiem character who was genuinely in love with his ghoul, and embraced her in the epilogue after the bloody in game revolution. The second was as part of an introduction for a new player into an ongoing requiem larp, which unlike the other attempts in said larp worked out quite well in the end. My longest running Dark Ages character embraced quite prolifically as both a reward for long standing retainers to leave capable managers behind in the various territories we were visiting, as his intention was to establish a vast number of Obertus abbeys post bitter crusade to protect various books and knowledge. At least one of them had been killed by the Inquisition by the time the game ended, sadly, just as we were about to rescue him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1060-kale-fangblade","name":"Kale Fangblade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1060_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-21T14:25:59-07:00","id":1544431,"title":"","content":"Played a sabbat lasombra who volunteers for mass embraces to bolster her position. She tends to single out woman of simular age to her and is quite supportive as much as you can be. Providing insight into obtenerbration and emotional support, partly to give herself a slight edge in clan by having childer who dont hate her.<br /> <br /> &quot;The shadow must grow...and deepen.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 10-21-2024, 05:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-22T06:24:03-07:00","id":1544458,"title":"","content":"Well I tend to see cuddles as something that happens to other supernatural beings, but every so often you just have to win a fight with a grizzly bear (or a Malkavian wilfully misunderstands a fellow\u2019s concept of personal space, possibly for Fun &amp; Profit).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-25T09:03:05-07:00","id":1544729,"title":"","content":"Oh yes! My Lasombra embraced a run away ghoul that fled the local chantry. She had two reasons for doing so :<br /> <br /> - First the ghoul had 10 years of experience and managed to flee the chantry, my character admired her a lot for it. It showed she had enough willpower to at least try to fight back.<br /> - Secondly, the ghoul\u2019s master had made a move against my character in the past and this was my character\u2019s way of getting back at him.<br /> <br /> She first asked the ghoul if she wanted a way to protect herself against her former master, by joining her clan. Which she obviously accepted. My character then asked the prince in private to be allowed to sire a childe, and managed to convince him to keep it a secret for the next Elysium. The prince, a Toreador who had a beef with the tremere loved the idea.<br /> <br /> So in the end my Lasombra attended the next elysium with her new childe. The tremere almost frenzied due to the provocation, but unfortunately he managed to keep is cool and endure the humiliation. Thanks for my character, the prince loved it!<br /> <br /> As for handling the childe mechanically, i purchased a Mawla at 1 dot since we were playing V5. There\u2019s probably some kind of advantage that could represent this in previous editions, it\u2019s been ages since I\u2019ve touched any of them. The DM would play her as an NPC.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26771-algarik","name":"Algarik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26771_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}